  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast bias when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) — model tends to overestimate prices.",
    "Adjust downward for recent spikes (last 5-7 days) — model often overshoots after sharp increases.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction if forecast is > 10% above recent 30-day average — especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Increase downward bias if sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0) and price is trending downward — model underestimates downside risk.",
    "Lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast 1-2 days prior, reduce next-day forecast by 5-10% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "Avoid overreacting to single-day sentiment spikes — apply smoothing filter (e.g., 3-day moving average) to sentiment before adjusting forecasts."
  ]
}
